@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:architecture;performance] universal-foliage-pipeline
ALL current and future vegetation (trees, palms, bushes, hedges, flowers, grass,
groundcover and vegetation embedded in mixed meshes), in every region and import
namespace, MUST pass through foliage_system's build-time classification, bounded
representation generation and validation, and UYorimichiFoliageSubsystem at runtime.
New vegetation MUST declare recognizable foliage material/asset semantics or certified per-face roles; hiding
foliage inside an unclassified material or bypassing the registry is forbidden.
Explicit rigid role certification is only for non-vegetation surfaces (such as fruit reusing leaf paint),
never an exemption for vegetation or an optimization fallback.
Missing, stale or invalid representations MUST fail the normal build and gameplay
readiness, never silently render an unoptimized fallback. Preparation and all cooked
dependencies MUST belong to the normal incremental build graph.
The persistent graphics switch MUST restore the original rendering when disabled;
both modes MUST remain managed by the same subsystem. Switching MUST preserve authored
placements, collision, camera visibility behavior and gameplay, without a restart.
Indivisible textured plant props MAY retain authored surfaces only through the shared,
explicit authored-prop policy and its hard whole-mesh budget; this MUST NOT become a
fallback for unclassified sources or the policy for dense vegetation.
Visual and shadow representations MUST have separate budgets; distant forest patches
MUST preserve silhouettes and clearings. Changes MUST carry revision-bound ground,
canopy and aerial captures plus real-time frame/GPU timings before performance or
visual-equivalence claims. Detached cosmetic particles are not vegetation placements.
